  https://github.com/ACCESS-NRI/access-om3-configs/archive/refs/tags/release-MCW_100km_era_iaf-1.0-beta.tar.gz
abstract: >-
  This is a development model configuration of ACCESS-OM3
  with coupled ocean waves (MCW: MOM6, CICE6 and WW3). This
  uses a release of the ACCESS-OM3 software (version
  2026.05.004), a global grid with 100km nominal resolution,
  bathymetry generated from GEBCO 2024 and ocean initial
  conditions generated from WOA2023. Interannual Forcing
  (IAF) from hourly ERA5 atmospheric reanalysis, with
  JRA55-do v1.6 river and land-ice runoff, is used as input
  data.

  WW3 waves are coupled to the ocean, where surface Stokes
  drift is used for Langmuir turbulence in the ePBL mixing
  scheme, and to the sea ice, which uses C-grid dynamics
  with a floe size distribution. The coupling interval, CICE
  timestep and MOM6 baroclinic timestep are 1800 s.

  ACCESS-OM3 is the third generation of the ACCESS global
  ocean-seaice model. It uses up to date releases of the
  MOM6 ocean model and CICE6 sea-ice model, and adds the
  WAVEWATCH III (WW3) wave model in this configuration. It
  is the first ACCESS model release using CMEPS (Community
  Mediator for Earth Prediction Systems), built on top of
  NUOPC (National Unified Operational Prediction
  Capability), infrastructure to connect these model
  components.
